# Standby and screen off

Wake sources (Home Assistant, proximity, face) are in `standby-wake-sources-context.mdc`. This rule is the countdown and the screen-off path those sources sit on.

## How standby works

- The player never lets Android turn the screen off on its own: `MainActivity` sets `FLAG_KEEP_SCREEN_ON`.
- After `standbyMinutes` with no touch, `PlayerViewModel.setAwake(false)` drops window brightness to `standbyBrightness` (floor `0.01`, so the backlight stays on). At standby brightness 0, `PlayerScreen` also draws a full-screen black box (`ViewState.isBlackout`). On AMOLED that looks fully off; on LCD the backlight still glows.
- With `ScreenSettings.standbyScreenOff` and a device admin, standby calls `DevicePolicyManager.lockNow()` instead. The editor checkbox is under Standby; the HA switch is `standby_screen_off`. Default is false.

## Settings are not a touch

- The add-on sends `ServerMessage.Settings` on every reconnect, layout save, HA settings patch, and preview. Those used to call `onUserInteraction()`, so the countdown never finished.
- `onServerSettings` stores the settings without waking. It restarts the clocks only when `standbyMinutes` or `backToHomeSeconds` changed. Standby turned off (`standbyMinutes == 0`) while asleep does wake the screen. The tablet's own settings dialog (`applyScreenSettings`) still counts as a touch.
- Still restart the countdown: touches, alerts and overlays, `OpenPage`, `Wake(true)`, identify.

## Turning the screen off

- `ScreenPowerRepository.turnScreenOff()` takes a partial wake lock (so the WebSocket survives and HA can wake the tablet) then `lockNow()`. `turnScreenOn()` takes a 5 s `SCREEN_BRIGHT_WAKE_LOCK | ACQUIRE_CAUSES_WAKEUP` and drops the partial lock. `canTurnScreenOff()` accepts `ScreenOffAdminReceiver` or the kiosk `LockTaskDeviceAdminReceiver`.
- `updateScreenPower()` runs when awake changes and when `standbyScreenOff` or the wake-source settings change. When face wake is usable it skips `lockNow()` and stays on the software blackout, because the camera often dies with the panel off. Proximity-only may still turn the screen off.
- `onResumed()` treats a resume while `isScreenOff` as a power-button wake. `MainActivity.showOverLockScreen()` (`setShowWhenLocked(true)`) shows the player instead of the keyguard.
- Without an admin, standby falls back to dimming. The settings dialog offers "Allow turning the screen off in standby" (`ACTION_ADD_DEVICE_ADMIN`) when the setting is on and no admin is active.
- A screen that is off cannot be woken by touch. Wake it with the power button, `remote_screens.wake`, an alert, or `OpenPage`.

## Diagnosing standby on a tablet

- Release builds print no app logs (Timber is debug only). A debug build signed with the local debug key installs over a debug-key-signed release with `adb install -r` and keeps the pairing.
- Debug lines in `PlayerViewModel`: `Standby clock restarted`, `Awake`. Read them with `adb logcat -d -v time -s PlayerViewModel`.
- Window brightness: `adb shell dumpsys window` and look for `sbrt` on `MainActivity` (`sbrt=1.0` is awake at 100%).
- A countdown whose deadline jumps back up was cancelled and relaunched. Phantom touches show up in `adb shell getevent -lt`.
- The partial wake lock is fine while plugged in. On battery, Doze can still drop the connection, and the screen then wakes only from the power button.
